Subject: Deferred counting: the smallest reconcile limit is 256 zero-count objects (was 4096)

What this does
  - quickjs.c: `js_drc_minlim` (the floor of `rt->zct_limit`, read at the two places that set the limit) defaults to 256 instead of 4096. The
    `QJS_DRC_MINLIM` environment knob is unchanged.

Why we need it
  Earleyboyer (eb-det): -3.2% cycles and -30% LLC load misses (19.0 M -> 13.2 M); the cycles plateau runs from 2048 down to 64, best at
  128-256. Frees run while the freed cells and their children are still cached, and allocation reuses hot blocks from the block cache
  (reviewer MSG 667/668).

Soundness
  A tuning constant only: the limit decides when a reconcile runs, never what it frees.

Failure modes
  The cost moves to more frequent reconcile scans on workloads with deep stacks (the scan is O(roots) per reconcile). Instructions rise
  0.4% on eb-det. Check alloc-heavy kernels and one deep-recursion case at the end pass; the fallback is a per-unit setting at unit init.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -4568 +4568 @@
-static uint32_t js_drc_minlim = 4096;
+static uint32_t js_drc_minlim = 256;
